  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 301 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nTUESDAY AND TUESDAY NIGHT:\n\nSkies will clear from west to east during the day and \ntemperatures will trend warmer in the wake of the warm front. \nLook for highs Tuesday to reach the middle 60s to middle 70s, \naround 10-15 degrees above normal. Gusty southerly winds are \nexpected over northwest Wisconsin into the I-35 corridor of \nMinnesota as the low-level jet gradually weakens and pushes \neastward during the day. Gusts of 15-25 mph are expected with \nthe highest values east of a Hayward to Bayfield line.\n\nA cold front will advance southeastward across northern \nMinnesota into northwest Wisconsin by early Tuesday evening. \nWinds will veer northwesterly behind the cold front and will \ngradually weaken during the evening. Low temps will be in the \nupper 30s to middle 40s.\n\nWEDNESDAY THROUGH FRIDAY NIGHT:\n\nNorthwest flow is forecast in the wake of Tuesday's cold front.\nTemperatures will cool slightly while remaining several degrees\nabove normal. Diurnal shower chances are expected as colder air\naloft advects east-southeast over the Northland. Highs will be \nin the low 60s to near 70 on Wednesday then upper 50s to middle \n60s Thursday and Friday.\n\nSATURDAY INTO EARLY NEXT WEEK:\n\nA more unsettled pattern takes shape Saturday into early next \nweek. Guidance indicates an upper-level ridge will move into the\nnorthern Plains and Canadian Prairies Friday night and Saturday\nmorning. A low pressure system is forecast to develop over \neastern Montana and ride northeastward toward James Bay by \nSunday morning. That progression will pull another warm front \nnorthward across the region with temperatures climbing well \nabove normal for Saturday. Light rain showers are possible ahead\nof the front Saturday. A cool front will follow on Sunday and \nwill stall out over the Upper Midwest Sunday night and Monday \nleaving a baroclinic zone in place across Minnesota and \nWisconsin. Widespread shower chances are forecast Sunday through\nTuesday.",
